---
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
---

<section class="container features">
  <div class="intro">
    <h2>What the tunnel handles for you.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="cell">
      <svg
        width="26"
        height="26"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--nh-accent)"
        stroke-width="1.8"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="2" />
        <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4" />
      </svg>
      <h3>Real HTTPS, trusted once</h3>
      <p>
        Secure cookies, OAuth callbacks and service workers need HTTPS, so every alias gets a real
        certificate. Nearhost creates its own local CA on first run and you trust it once. No shared
        key ships in the binary, so nobody else can mint certificates for your <code>.test</code>{' '}
        names.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href={url('/docs/concepts/tls-and-the-proxy/')}>
        TLS and the proxy
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <svg
        width="26"
        height="26"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--nh-accent)"
        stroke-width="1.8"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7z" />
      </svg>
      <h3>Hot reload and WebSockets pass through</h3>
      <p>
        Nearhost can forward a dev server's port to the same number on your laptop. Asset URLs that
        point at <code>localhost</code> still resolve, so hot reload connects with the remote config
        untouched.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href={url('/docs/concepts/dev-servers-and-hot-reload/')}>
        Dev servers and hot reload
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <svg
        width="26"
        height="26"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--nh-accent)"
        stroke-width="1.8"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7" />
        <path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5" />
      </svg>
      <h3>Port discovery</h3>
      <p>
        Nearhost reads port variables from <code>.env</code>. Presets from a registry you choose to
        trust add Compose, Vite and Laravel Sail, and warn about port clashes and a missing{' '}
        <code>allowedHosts</code> before you start. For anything else, give it the web port.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href={url('/docs/concepts/discovery/')}>
        How discovery works
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <svg
        width="26"
        height="26"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--nh-accent)"
        stroke-width="1.8"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M4 17l6-6-6-6M12 19h8" />
      </svg>
      <h3>Runs on your SSH config</h3>
      <p>
        Nearhost shells out to OpenSSH, so <code>Include</code>, <code>Match</code>, ProxyJump,
        agent forwarding and keychain identities apply. It stores nothing but the host name.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href={url('/docs/concepts/ssh-transport/')}>
        SSH transport
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <svg
        width="26"
        height="26"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--nh-accent)"
        stroke-width="1.8"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="14" rx="2" />
        <path d="M8 21h8M12 18v3" />
      </svg>
      <h3>Local projects too</h3>
      <p>
        The <code>local</code> server needs no setup. Projects on your laptop get the same alias and
        certificate, so one tool covers the laptop and the servers.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href={url('/docs/getting-started/add-a-project/')}>
        Add a project
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <svg
        width="26"
        height="26"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--nh-accent)"
        stroke-width="1.8"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M12 3v18M3 12h18" />
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
      </svg>
      <h3>Headless when you want it</h3>
      <p>
        <code>nearhost up</code> starts projects without the UI. <code>nearhost doctor</code> checks
        ports, trust, hosts and each server. Config is one YAML file you can edit by hand.
      </p>
      <a class="more" href={url('/docs/reference/cli/')}>
        CLI reference
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .more {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 4px;
    color: var(--nh-accent);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .more:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .features {
    padding-block: var(--nh-section);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 48px;
  }
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--nh-font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: var(--nh-track-display);
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--nh-line);
    border: 1px solid var(--nh-line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 32px;
    background: var(--nh-ground);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--nh-muted);
    font-size: 15.5px;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--nh-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 719px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .cell {
      padding: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>
